  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "They were chasing after the second inning. Down four, fighting through ten. And refused to fold when it mattered most.",
    "what_this_means": "Tatis powered the early swings with his bat, but Petro Park's late-inning currents belong to Machado now. Two runners tied the game in the ninth. One more inning and he walked it off. That's the game right there: the offense found something in the middle innings, the bullpen held the door, and when the tenth came around, one swing ended it. This is a team that converts runners on base into actual results when the margin collapses to nothing. Eight left on base yesterday. Four of them scored. That's execution under pressure. Not a luxury, not a pattern yet, just what happened when it mattered. Machado's moment in the tenth is the kind of at-bat that separates survival from sequence.",
    "what_to_watch": "Mart\u00edn P\u00e9rez takes the mound for Atlanta tonight with a 2.78 ERA, but he's given up five runs in five innings across his last two starts. JP Sears gets the ball for San Diego. A chance to build on what the bullpen protected last night.",
